`USE_X86_64_ASM` is not define anywhere, so the specific assembly optimizations are unused. We can keep it for the sake of compatibility with Bullet code, but it would be good to add a comment about it.

Here's the comment in Bullet:
```
// The definition of USE_X86_64_ASM is moved into the build system. You can enable it manually by commenting out the following lines
//#if (defined(__GNUC__) && defined(__x86_64__) && !defined(__ICL))  // || (defined(__ICL) && defined(_M_X64))   bug in Intel compiler, disable inline assembly
//	#define USE_X86_64_ASM
//#endif
```

So we could have something like that instead:
```
// -- GODOT start --
// Assembly optimizations are not used at the moment.
//#define USE_X86_64_ASM
// -- GODOT end --
```
